{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Create two new external Go module libraries: a general-purpose library (fabric-lib-go style) hosting gossip protoext/discovery utilities, cauthdsl policy utilities, ccprovider structures, ledger interfaces and common utilities (U1-U5), and a configuration library (fabric-config style) hosting configtxgen and configtxlator/protolator functionality (U7-U8).",
    "Extract code from the hyperledger/fabric v2.x code base as the source of truth, preserving exported API signatures as far as practical to minimize changes in consumers.",
    "Depend on the published hyperledger/fabric-protos-go module for generated protobuf types instead of vendoring .proto files or generated code into the new libraries.",
    "Use Go modules (go.mod) with semantic versioning (initial release v1.0.0) for both new libraries; consumers (fabric-sdk-go) pin versions rather than vendoring copies.",
    "Apply Apache-2.0 license headers, DCO sign-off, README/godoc documentation and a CI pipeline (build, unit tests, lint/vet, minimum coverage) to each new repository.",
    "For U6, implement the go.mod honoring workaround inside the Fabric Go chaincode platform build logic: detect a go.mod file in the chaincode package and copy it into the build context so module builds work; mark it clearly as a temporary, deprecated behavior in code comments and docs.",
    "Update fabric-sdk-go to delete its internal/ and third_party/ copies and import the new external libraries instead, including rewiring the discovery client and resource/configtx.go.",
    "Keep extraction changes minimal and mechanical (no functional redesign) to limit regression risk; only adjust imports, visibility and package layout."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "One senior Go developer performs all work; estimates include the developer's own unit testing and self-review but exclude review time of other maintainers.",
    "The hyperledger/fabric repository (v2.x stream) and fabric-sdk-go repository are available and build locally; no changes to protobuf definitions are required.",
    "Existing unit tests travel with the extracted packages and only need import/path adaptation.",
    "fabric-sdk-go already has Docker-based integration test infrastructure that can be run to validate the migration.",
    "New repositories (hosting, CI minutes, branch protection) can be provisioned without significant organizational delay.",
    "U6 is intentionally short-lived; only a minimal implementation plus deprecation note is required, no long-term support or extensive configuration surface.",
    "Effort covers development, unit tests, SDK migration, integration/regression verification, documentation and release tagging for the complete increment; no end-user application migration is in scope."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Repository, module and CI setup for new shared libraries",
      "activity_description": "Provision the two new repositories, initialize go.mod, add license/DCO/contribution files, set up CI (build, vet/lint, unit tests, coverage) and release/versioning conventions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Externalize gossip protoext and discovery utilities",
      "activity_description": "Extract gossip protoext utilities and the discovery-client-dependent gossip helper code into the general library, rewire generated protobuf references to fabric-protos-go, adapt imports and port/adapt unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2: Externalize cauthdsl policy utilities",
      "activity_description": "Extract cauthdsl policy parsing/compilation utilities (and minimal protoutil dependencies) into the general library, clean up imports and port/adapt unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U3: Externalize ccprovider structures",
      "activity_description": "Extract ccprovider structures such as ChaincodeData, chaincode package parsing (tar/gzip) and deployment spec types into the general library, adapting imports and unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U4: Externalize ledger structures",
      "activity_description": "Extract commonly used ledger interfaces/types and ledger utilities needed by clients into the general library, adapting imports and unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U5: Externalize common utilities",
      "activity_description": "Extract common utilities (flogging with zap integration, crypto helpers, util, viperutil, genesis block helpers, etc.) into the general library, resolving interdependencies and porting/adapting unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7: Externalize configtxgen functions",
      "activity_description": "Extract configtxgen functionality into the configuration library with a clean programmatic API (channel creation transactions, org/consortium definitions), replacing SDK-internal copies; port and extend unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8: Externalize configtxlator/protolator functions",
      "activity_description": "Extract configtxlator/protolator deep-marshaling functionality into the configuration library, adapt imports and port/adapt unit tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "U6: Temporary go.mod honoring in Go chaincode build",
      "activity_description": "Modify the Go chaincode platform build logic to detect and copy a go.mod file from the chaincode package into the build context, add tests and mark the behavior as deprecated/temporary in code and docs.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Migrate fabric-sdk-go to the external libraries",
      "activity_description": "Remove the SDK's internal/ and third_party/ copies, add module dependencies on the new libraries, rewire the discovery client and resource/configtx.go to the external configtxgen/configtxlator APIs, and fix all compile issues.",
      "most_likely_effort": 8
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Integration and regression verification",
      "activity_description": "Run and fix unit and Docker-based integration test suites across the new libraries and fabric-sdk-go, update CI pipelines, and resolve defects uncovered during verification.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A12",
      "activity_name": "Documentation and release",
      "activity_description": "Write README/godoc and migration notes for SDK consumers, document the U6 deprecation, tag v1.0.0 releases of the new libraries and produce release notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 56
  }
}
```

